":33.5,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.15891671760957402,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":68.9,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.05934360588196408,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":25.8,"_gate_piotroski":6,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":66.7,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.11402846821218482,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":85.6,"_gate_rev_durability":0.24148963665088052,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.019776275165764304,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":33.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.07663449068717698,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.017927041468409788,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":70.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.04618,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":30.8,"_gate_insider_buying":0.056,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":5.6,"pf":[],"description_full":"Business First Bancshares, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for b1BANK that provides various banking products and services in Louisiana and Texas. It offers various deposit products and services, including checking and savings, time, and money market accounts; and certificates of deposits, remote deposit capture, and direct deposit services. The company also provides commercial and industrial loans, such as working capital, term, equipment financing, asset acquisition, expansion and development, borrowing base, and other loan products, as well as commercial lines of credit, accounts receivable factoring, agricultural financing, and letters of credit; construction and development loans; commercial real estate loans; residential real estate loans comprising first and second lien 1-4 family mortgage loans, and home equity lines of credit; and consumer loans, including secured and unsecured installment, and term loans. In addition, it offers wealth management products, including mutual funds, annuities, individual retirement accounts, and other financial products, as well as other fiduciary and private banking products and services. Further, the company provides a range of other financial services comprising debit and credit cards, treasury and cash management, merchant, automated clearing house, lock-box, receivables factoring, correspondent banking, and other treasury services, as well as employee and payroll benefits solutions; and drive-through banking facilities, automated teller machines, night depository, personalized checks, electronic funds transfer, domestic and foreign wire transfer, traveler's checks, vault, loan and deposit sweep accounts, interest-rate swaps, small business administration products, online and mobile banking, e-statements, and bank-by-mail services. Business First Bancshares, Inc. was incorporated in 2006 and is headquartered in Baton Rouge, Louisiana.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David R. Melville III | Chairman, President & CEO | Age 50 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 821 people. Revenue per employee of $395K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 24%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $112K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Business First Bancshares, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.0B market cap on $325M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +12% over the past three years and +24% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 17% against a 9% cost of capital, a 8-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $92M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 28 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.05\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 2.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 4.6% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.003403867073730756},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (94% sell ratio, net $4.0M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 61% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Head-To-Head Contrast: Business First Bancshares (NASDAQ:BFST) vs. Community Trust Bancorp (NASDAQ:CTBI)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/head-to-head-contrast-business-first-bancshares-nasdaqbfst-vs-community-trust-bancorp-nasdaqctbi.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794438899.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.92,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(BFST) as a Liquidity Pulse for Institutional Tactics","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/16/BFST_as_a_Liquidity_Pulse_for_Institutional_Tactics_111026025002_1794297002.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794297002.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Earnings And Dividend Update Could Be A Game Changer For Business First Bancshares Stock (BFST)","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-bfst/business-first-bancshares/news/earnings-and-dividend-update-could-be-a-game-changer-for-bus","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793774505.752,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.92,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"Business First Bancshares (BFST) Earnings And Buybacks Put Its Undervalued Story To The Test","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-bfst/business-first-bancshares/news